<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Tauri shell (Contents/MacOS/Marquee) entitlements — intentionally empty.
       The Tauri/WebKit shell is a self-contained binary that loads only
       Apple-signed or Developer-ID-signed Tauri plugin libraries. It does not
       dlopen any third-party library at runtime, so library-validation (the
       default hardened-runtime restriction) is not a problem.

       No sandbox: Marquee is distributed direct-download, not via the App Store.
       File access works via the Tauri dialog plugin and full-disk Finder paths.
       Child process spawn (→ slideshow-gen sidecar) is allowed by default under
       the hardened runtime — no extra entitlement required.

       If the notary log names a missing entitlement, add only that one here. -->
</dict>
</plist>
